    "insights": [
      "Result follows entirely from Mathlib hasSum_zeta_two (Basel ζ(2)=π²/6); the only content is the even/odd parity decomposition plus the arithmetic π²/6 − π²/24 = π²/8.",
      "HasSum.even_add_odd is the precise tool: splits a HasSum over ℕ into even- and odd-indexed subsequences, exactly matching the parity split needed.",
      "Even part handled by rescaling: 1/(2k)² = (1/4)·1/k², so HasSum.mul_left gives the even-square sum value π²/24 directly.",
      "Odd value pinned by HasSum.unique (even+odd reconstructs the whole; whole and even values known) rather than computed directly.",
      "This is the λ(2)=(3/4)ζ(2)=π²/8 special value of the Dirichlet lambda function λ(s)=(1−2^{-s})ζ(s)."
    ],
    "mathlibGaps": [
      "No gap: hasSum_zeta_two and HasSum.even_add_odd already in Mathlib; full result is an elementary corollary."
    ],
